QUESTION [header: "Fix direction"]:
  GNOME/mutter gives every native Wayland toplevel keyboard focus when it
  maps — there is no client-side opt-out (unlike niri's "open-focused false"
  window rule). Which fix do you want?

OPTION 1 (recommended): "XWayland fallback (Recommended)"
  description:
    On GNOME, keebs creates the OSK as an XWayland window with
    override-redirect + no-focus hints — exactly the window type that worked
    yesterday. Native Wayland window stays for niri. Proven, small, immediate.
  preview:
    // osk_main.rs + render.rs
    if std::env::var("XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP")
        .map(|d| d.contains("GNOME"))
        .unwrap_or(false)
    {
        // mutter focuses every xdg_toplevel; only an
        // override-redirect X11 window can opt out.
        std::env::set_var("SDL_VIDEODRIVER", "x11");
        // + X11::XSetWindowAttributes override-redirect,
        // WM_HINTS input=false, skip-taskbar
    }
    // else: native Wayland + niri window-rule (open-focused false)

OPTION 2: "Subsurface rewrite"
  description:
    OSK becomes a wl_subsurface over a tiny hidden toplevel — subsurfaces
    never get keyboard focus on any compositor. Fully pure-Wayland, but needs
    hand-rolled libwayland protocol code and is untested territory
    (rendering/input risk).
  preview:
    // render.rs — pure Wayland, no X11
    // 1. create 1x1 hidden toplevel (parent)
    // 2. OSK window: SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND
    //    _SURFACE_ROLE_CUSTOM_BOOLEAN = true
    // 3. dlopen libwayland-client:
    //    wl_subcompositor_get_subsurface(
    //        osk_surface, parent_surface)
    // 4. sync position per frame (wl_subsurface.set_position)
    // keyboard focus: never leaves the target app OK

OPTION 3: "GNOME Shell extension"
  description:
    keebs stays pure Wayland; a tiny GNOME Shell extension watches for the
    keebs.osk window and re-focuses whatever was focused before it.
    Compositor-side fix, but a new artifact to maintain in the Flake and it
    can't be tested from here.
  preview:
    // Flake: new extension package + gnome.shell.enableExtension
    // extension.js:
    const prev = display.focus_window;
    global.compositor.connect('window-created', w => {
      if (w.get_app_id() === 'keebs.osk')
        prev?.activate();
      // also re-focus on OSK show/hide cycle
    });
    // keebs code: unchanged

